<title>USA: United hopeful of a flight attendants pact.</title>
<headline>United hopeful of a flight attendants pact.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines was hopeful of reaching a labor deal soon with its flight attendants, the carrier's president, John Edwardson, said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm confident at this point that when we get together next month we'll continue to make progress,&quot; said Edwardson who was in town to testify before a Congressional subcommittee on airport landing slots.</p>
<p>United, with 21,000 flight attendants, is a unit of UAL Corp. The Association of Flight Attendants is reviewing the latest UAL proposal, with talks slated to resume in June in Honolulu.</p>
</text>
